# .trivyignore
# OS-level CVEs in python:3.9-slim (debian 13.1) base image.
# These are in system packages (openssl, glibc, ncurses, systemd, libcap)
# with no available fix in the debian 13 package repository as of 2026-05-10.
# Tracked for remediation — will update base image digest when debian patches land.
# Re-evaluate when running: trivy image --severity HIGH,CRITICAL python:3.9-slim

# glibc integer overflow
CVE-2026-0861

# libcap TOCTOU race condition (no fix available)
CVE-2026-4878

# ncurses buffer overflow (no fix available)
CVE-2025-69720

# openssl CVEs - fixed versions exist but not yet in debian 13 repo
CVE-2025-15467
CVE-2026-31789
CVE-2025-69419
CVE-2025-69421
CVE-2026-28387
CVE-2026-28388
CVE-2026-28389
CVE-2026-28390

# systemd IPC vulnerability (no fix available)
CVE-2026-29111

# setuptools vendored dependency CVEs.
# jaraco.context and wheel are bundled INSIDE setuptools' own vendor directory
# for setuptools' internal use only — they are not accessible to application code.
# The standalone wheel package has been upgraded to 0.46.2 (clean).
# These vendored copies can only be fixed by a setuptools release that updates
# its internal vendor bundle — not by upgrading the packages themselves.
CVE-2026-23949
CVE-2026-24049
